From 9937866c39fbfd92e6a23ebb564285a3b372d2aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon <jon@pionex.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:54:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] drm/imagination: add BXM-4-64 revision 36.56.104.183 as
 experimental

The Allwinner A733 (sun60i) integrates a PowerVR BXM-4-64 MC1 at BVNC
36.56.104.183 -- one silicon revision from the 36.52.104.182 already handled
here for the T-HEAD TH1520.

Nothing else is missing for this part: Imagination's firmware tree carries
open-ABI firmware for exactly this revision (powervr/rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw,
version 1.1.OS@6976702, PVR_FW_INFO_VERSION 3 with PVR_FW_FLAGS_OPEN_SOURCE,
packed BVNC matching the hardware), and Mesa's device table already knows the
GPU ID (0x36104183, src/imagination/common/device_info/bxm-4-64.h). Today the
kernel is the only component that refuses the part: pvr_gpu_support_level()
returns PVR_GPU_UNKNOWN, so probe fails with -ENODEV unless the user passes
exp_hw_support=1.

List it as experimental first. Following the 36.52.104.182 precedent it can be
promoted to PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED once a Vulkan CTS run has been made on the
hardware.

Hardware: Radxa Cubie A7A, Allwinner A733, GPU BVNC 36.56.104.183.

Signed-off-by: Jon <jon@pionex.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
index 54fe418..6be7fc9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -535,6 +535,9 @@ pvr_gpu_support_level(const struct pvr_gpu_id *gpu_id)
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
 		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
 
+	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 56, 104, 183):
+		return PVR_GPU_EXPERIMENTAL;
+
 	default:
 		return PVR_GPU_UNKNOWN;
 	}
